WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.640
Now, what does it mean, Barah? Barah means to create. What does it mean to create? To create, in Hebrew, there are two words.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.060
Yassar and Barah.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.040
Yassar means to create something which is concretely.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.020
You see?

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.820
Obedience says Yasser or.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.740
Create something which is concretely.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.720
Something that you could perceive.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:33.120
But what you say, Yasser or.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.340
What is the Hosea?

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.940
Hosea is the actual something.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.380
Something which is difficult to conceive.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.660
In other words, you don't see Hosea.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:43.300
You don't see.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.720
And that's why there is Hosea.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.500
So that's why it's Barah.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.980
Bara is something ephemeral, something which is difficult to grasp.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.020
And why is it difficult to grasp?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.600
You're going to see this later on.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.320
Why is this so difficult to grasp?

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.580
In other words, what God created at the beginning is not a concrete world.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.200
It's not something complete that you could grasp,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.940
but rather something which is a phenomenon, something which is occurring.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.080
It's difficult to grasp.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:08.900
And you're going to see why.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.360
Because the world, as I'm going to say very clearly, was told by all.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.800
So therefore, the beginning was only bara.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.800
And after bara, there was asiyah and there was yesirah or whatever you want to call it.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.800
But the very beginning, the substractum of things, was only bara.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.800
So, Bereshit bara Elohim, etashamayim eta ares, heavens and earth.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.800
What does it mean shamayim? It means the mal'akhim. What does it mean?

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.800
Later on the Torah is going to make it clear that the word shamayim doesn't mean nothing supernatural.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.800
It means just the firmament, just, you know, the atmosphere around you, that is where it comes from.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.800
The word is beyond the Arabic, means this Arabic. What happened with the other worlds?

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.800
Ramban says very clear, the Torah doesn't tell you because that's not relevant to us.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.800
We have to understand about the world we live, because the Torah comes to answer only so far as we're concerned.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:59.800
Other questions, they are not answered by the Torah, because they are not relevant to everyone.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.800
Maybe you as an individual, as a philosopher, you may answer, but that's not the Torah problem.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.800
You could get maybe in Kabbalah, but the Torah comes to answer to the common person, to everyone.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.540
later on it will be, what is the Shamayim?

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.700
Layikra Elohim Barakiyah

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.860
Shamayim.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.440
It's nothing Barakiyah. This is the same Barakiyah.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.740
What happened to the other thing?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.620
If you want the other things, you have to go more

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.380
deeper than from Mash. You have to go and

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.720
take other things. Mr. Shapo, do you want to do?

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.640
There seems to be an apparent contradiction.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:29.400
How?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.320
Barak Elohim, Barak.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.060
Ephemeral, intangible,

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.120
Shamayim. No, it's not tangible.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.380
It's the other one. Intangible, I said.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.380
Intangible.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.380
The earth is tangible.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.380
No, you're going to see that now.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.380
Very good, I like your point.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.380
But you're going to see immediately that this is not the case.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.380
That when there was Bara'a, it was not tangible.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.380
So now, the Sheba...

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.380
If Bara'a became tangible?

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:51.380
Yes, we're going to see how.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.380
Very simple.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.380
If Bara'a became tangible, was it tangible?

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.380
Well, not necessarily because it says about

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.400
about my right,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:58.740
I will imitate

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.740
the Taninim again on him.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.740
That was very distracting.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:01.160
You see?

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:01.820
My right,

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:02.500
I will imitate Adam.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.140
The first time was

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:03.980
Bediah, Adam.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:04.820
And it was from

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:05.920
Hathar, Adamah.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:08.960
What is it?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:09.520
There is Yassar.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:10.680
There is Yassar

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.340
and there is Balaam.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.340
In Adam.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.100
Because in man

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:14.720
there is two parts.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.320
One tangible

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:15.940
and one tangible.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:17.500
That's why there is

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.300
Yassirah in Adam

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.440
and Bediah in Adam.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:20.820
And there is Shammah

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.580
which is intangible.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:22.480
You know?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.200
It's not tangible

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:23.720
to the Shammah.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.600
Now let me

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.280
say to this

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:33.560
May I continue, gentlemen, with the pesukim?

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.100
Now, yes.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:42.140
Nobody answered me.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.660
We don't know.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.720
No, I don't.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.940
As soon as you have an answer,

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.280
it means that God had to create the world.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.200
And we say that God created the world

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.640
out as an act of freedom.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.560
He didn't have to do it.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.920
So if you tell me why, then he doesn't have to do it.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:03:59.780
Then the world is a beginning.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.660
Why did he do it 5,000 years ago or 5 million years ago

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.780
or 5 billion years ago?

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.500
Should I have done it before?

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:06.900
We don't question that.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.140
So this is one point where man has to remove his shoes

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.940
and we don't...

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.340
Yes, sir.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.720
Doesn't it say in the Minhayon Kapurim

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.280
that God created the world because it was his will?

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:19.700
Of course.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.200
Iman Adiz deals with this.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.160
He said there was no reason.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.040
It was his will.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.800
That's the same thing. There's no reason.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.220
In other words, it's a nice way to say

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.380
we don't know.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.680
But it basically is that

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.620
we don't know and we don't try to possibly give a reason.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.600
But as soon as you give a reason,

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:40.760
why didn't you do it

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.960
a hundred

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:43.580
billion years ago?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.200
Whatever it was.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.640
The Chinese people.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:48.880
Yeah, Chinese people.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:51.960
Years and years

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.900
they don't have the religion

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:57.900
yet they are good to their fellow man, they believe in them, they respect their parents, they have no religion at all.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:03.900
Fine, fine, they have their own religion, they are going in. Would you consider them going in?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.900
Fine, but they have their own religion, they have ethics, they have their own religion.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:13.900
They are a government, you may have stated before, that they go in, have this, they believe in this, and they haven't got a fellow man.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:14.900
They believe in us.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.900
They have their own class, I know that, I understand that.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:18.900
But also he is coming soon.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.900
But he is safe.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.800
I don't know how well they got along with them, because, you know, I told them to learn.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.120
Now I'll tell you a little bit about the style of the Bible.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:31.580
It says,

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:35.860
Instead of beginning with Shammai, it begins always with the last word.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:38.580
Very important.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.260
God created it as Shammai with the others.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.240
How was it at the beginning of creation?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.580
There are Ares, Hayetah, Tohu, Baboh.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.360
What I'm going to tell you is difficult to understand, but it's simple also at the same time.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.540
Whenever you see something today,

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.900
whenever you see it, it accumulates upon the certain laws.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.920
You know, you see the change here, you know, this is blue, you know, the man is staying.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.320
Everything has an order.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.540
Today, everything I want you to see has an order.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.620
But when God created matter, substance,

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.160
that substance was completely, totally chaotic.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.560
There was no order.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:22.060
Now, our mind cannot understand this, cannot conceive this, because our mind is trained only to accommodate things and put them into some sort of order.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.840
At the beginning, there are Ares, Aeta, Tohu, Vavolu.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.120
No, even in the moon there is a kind of order.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.780
This, there was zero order.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.380
No order whatsoever.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.900
That's why it's a very young.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.480
Because it's so chaotic was.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.060
It wasn't important to have anything else.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:43.840
I beg your pardon?

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.540
It was not important to have it in any way.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.340
No, I tell you why I feel that this is...

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.280
Because nobody used it.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.480
No, not only that there was nothing to use it,

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.480
is that, for instance, let me give you an example.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.840
Today in matter, every substance has a form, has an order.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.960
You know, like this is the chair, it doesn't go wild, you know?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.640
But in those days, or rather at that moment,

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.100
the world was completely chaotic, mass.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.060
the whole substance was just going wild

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.420
in a way that you cannot determine it.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.080
It was completely chaos.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.160
That's why the beginning

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.840
was bara. By the way,

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.640
you know who is this? There is a very interesting

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.120
sympathetic commentator

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.460
which is not known because the book is very rare.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.460
His name is Shilomon Ben-Negar.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:28.140
He was from Turkey many years ago.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.880
It was about 500 years ago. And this is the

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.000
explanation that I give and it makes a lot of sense

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.040
to me. And I tell you why it makes sense to me.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:35.940
See, what you learn from here is something

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:39.540
very important, very deep, that it concerns us as human beings, besides as intelligent

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:45.920
human beings, it's just as simple human beings. It's the following. Matter, that's the Hiddur.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:52.980
As such, even that does have no order. There's no order in matter, the way God created it.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:08:01.560
So how order comes, order is a second step. In other words, do not think that nature by

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.020
itself has an order.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.700
No, sir. Even the whole

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.800
basis of order, you know,

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.700
is not just a natural or

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.580
automatic thing that

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:13.440
just happens this way.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.300
No, sir. Basically,

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.640
the world that

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.740
we are living in, the whole substance

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.300
of the world is a complete chaos.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.160
You know? But God

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.540
somehow superimposed as a

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.660
second stage, you know,

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.100
an order.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.460
Now, if you, and this order

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.460
is the word of God, or the laws that God

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.760
created to establish in

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.840
the physical world.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.420
Now, if somehow you would

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.340
remove the laws from the

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.520
physical world, the whole physical

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:44.680
world would be zoomed.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.860
Like an atomic bomb.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:48.940
I don't know how it would turn.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.340
You know, Jose de Alam,

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:52.740
that's what the Ginnah says,

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.700
if God would destroy the world, how would he destroy the world?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.240
Jose de Alam, let all

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.920
go. Which means,

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.240
you cannot describe it, because any

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.040
description is actually

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.260
follows a kind of order, a kind of

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.180
system. So therefore, let me

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.220
explain you one more detail

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.820
into this idea, which I think is very basic.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:12.520
God creates the world.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.320
This world, the basic thing

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.220
is completely chaotic. After

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.280
the chaos, God makes order.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:21.120
Likewise is also in the human world, I feel,

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.080
in the Torah. We're going to see in the book of

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:25.020
Elisha, God creates the human world also.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.980
And this human world is completely chaotic.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:27.560
Everybody,

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.300
everybody laughs like this.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:36.300
Later on, at the second stage, he makes, gives order, and that's the Torah.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:42.300
Now if you abandon the Torah, it's not that you have, you know, the abandonment of the Torah, it's not just you take a neutral position.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.300
No, no, that's not the case.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:52.300
If you abandon law, the essence of law is not just a neutral or aesthetic stage, but it's completely chaos.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.300
Right?

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:54.300
Sir?

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.300
So therefore you have the...

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.300
...

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:05.300
...

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:08.300
...

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:11.300
...

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:14.300
...

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.300
...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.300
...

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.300
...

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:35.560
Now, God says, what this Ha'aretz, this Ha'aretz, at the moment of Bani Yah, was created by God as Tohu B'Avohu, in the state of Tohu B'Avohu.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:36.720
Created as Tohu B'Avohu.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.320
Yes, yes, yes, this is it. This was created as Tohu B'Avohu.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.260
And later on, God says, Yini Or.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:48.040
Before that, if there isn't before, without that before, there was not even Tohu B'Avohu.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:48.980
Nothing, nothing.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:49.520
Zero.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:50.380
There was God.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:50.880
Nothingness.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.060
Nothingness. Zero.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:54.060
We don't know.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.060
I don't know. I should do it as well.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:58.060
There is nothing in the Tauhah Qawwah.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:00.060
When you say the Tauhah Qawwah is the absence of that,

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:05.060
the Tauhah Qawwah is the absence of the negative concept.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:09.060
So what's the absence of Tauhah Qawwah? What is that?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.060
There is no key.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:16.060
Gentlemen, gentlemen, one at a time.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.060
This young man has asked me a question,

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:21.060
and I'll have to repeat the same as what I said before.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.100
I mean, it is simply very simple.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.220
At the moment of creation,

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.200
we have got to do substance.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.420
Today when we see substance,

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.580
any substance that we see, it follows a kind of order.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.460
Even the widest of things

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.220
follows a kind of order. There is a system.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.500
Now, we would think

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.360
that this system

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.200
is intrinsic to the substance.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.580
You know, like the substance has three dimensions

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.060
and also has a dimension of order.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:49.800
I cannot quote.

