00:49:46.060 --> 00:50:06.940
Very good explanation, which I hope will come across when we study, you know, in the next

00:50:06.940 --> 00:50:09.920
Meanwhile, let me tell you the following.

00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:14.840
I'm going to be immediately with a class, rather than with a text,

00:50:15.040 --> 00:50:18.460
because probably in a few minutes people will be coming.

00:50:19.060 --> 00:50:27.100
So I was wondering whether we could answer some of the questions that you had from last week.

00:50:27.200 --> 00:50:28.880
I don't know, some of you maybe have some questions,

00:50:29.160 --> 00:50:34.360
either regarding last week's pedasha, what we studied last week,

00:50:34.360 --> 00:50:37.300
or, I don't know, something else.

00:50:37.400 --> 00:50:38.580
So if you have some questions,

00:50:38.720 --> 00:50:39.780
there are some subjects that you think

00:50:39.780 --> 00:50:41.020
that we could discuss,

00:50:41.640 --> 00:50:42.960
we would use a few minutes

00:50:42.960 --> 00:50:44.200
to discuss that particular subject.

00:50:44.320 --> 00:50:45.920
Is there any questions or anything that you...

00:50:45.920 --> 00:50:47.120
Yeah, briefly.

00:50:48.040 --> 00:50:51.000
I will tell you.

00:50:51.280 --> 00:50:54.020
The review, I will give you in a nutshell

00:50:54.020 --> 00:50:55.420
what we said last week.

00:50:56.800 --> 00:50:59.960
See, every book

00:50:59.960 --> 00:51:02.140
that is intelligently written

00:51:02.140 --> 00:51:06.620
that will make sure that the reader will know

00:51:06.620 --> 00:51:09.000
what are the basic assumptions that this book makes.

00:51:10.700 --> 00:51:11.560
It's very important.

00:51:12.220 --> 00:51:13.880
You cannot make any kind of judgment,

00:51:14.060 --> 00:51:15.540
you cannot develop any kind of thesis,

00:51:15.960 --> 00:51:17.180
if you don't make certain assumptions.

00:51:19.000 --> 00:51:21.800
Now, once that you understand these assumptions,

00:51:22.300 --> 00:51:24.360
then you can understand the reason or the rationale

00:51:24.360 --> 00:51:26.180
of that particular book.

00:51:26.180 --> 00:51:36.600
So the Torah must, as an intelligent book, must tell you what are the basic assumptions

00:51:36.600 --> 00:51:41.480
that we as a Jewish people, as people who will read and fulfill the Torah, must make.

00:51:43.440 --> 00:51:48.340
And if once that these assumptions are clear in our mind, we will be able to understand

00:51:48.340 --> 00:51:51.800
the main thesis of the book, of the 24 books of the Torah, the Rabbah Me'isri.

00:51:51.800 --> 00:51:57.340
So, what I said is that this perashah, the perashah Bereshit, comes to tell you what

00:51:57.340 --> 00:51:58.340
are the basic assumptions.

00:51:58.340 --> 00:52:06.340
And before I tell you what are the basic assumptions of the Torah, let me point to you what normally

00:52:06.340 --> 00:52:14.640
the non-Jewish world, whether scientific or philosophic, believes.

00:52:14.640 --> 00:52:18.480
The scientific and philosophic world believes that this is a thing as a universe.

00:52:18.480 --> 00:52:24.700
universe there are certain laws, physical laws. These physical laws are there from ever.

00:52:24.700 --> 00:52:31.080
Nobody made them in the sense that no, it was not the design of someone. They are there

00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:37.480
and they are uncreated, so to speak, and therefore the universe is what it is because it must

00:52:37.480 --> 00:52:42.580
be this way. There's no other way to be. And these laws are eternal, nobody could change

00:52:42.580 --> 00:52:44.660
them. So now,

00:52:45.780 --> 00:52:47.720
when they speak

00:52:47.720 --> 00:52:52.520
about God,

00:52:53.140 --> 00:52:53.820
a philosopher

00:52:53.820 --> 00:52:55.740
or a scientist,

00:52:56.260 --> 00:52:58.440
he means that there is a power

00:52:58.440 --> 00:53:00.300
behind these rules,

00:53:00.800 --> 00:53:02.420
but this power is not omnipotent,

00:53:02.500 --> 00:53:03.580
cannot do anything at once.

00:53:04.480 --> 00:53:06.240
You know, it's just like you have a machine

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:08.200
and you can know how to manipulate the machine,

00:53:08.300 --> 00:53:10.640
but if the machine is an airplane, you can use it as a submarine.

00:53:11.460 --> 00:53:12.360
So the same thing with the

00:53:12.360 --> 00:53:16.540
universe with certain laws, this is very, very big, maybe there is someone operating

00:53:16.540 --> 00:53:20.300
this machine, but he cannot do whatever he wants with this machine. Just like if you

00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:24.320
have a submarine, you cannot fly with a submarine, no matter how

00:53:24.320 --> 00:53:27.700
clever you are. This is basically the whole idea

00:53:27.700 --> 00:53:31.960
of God in non-Jewish thought,

00:53:32.500 --> 00:53:36.140
whether philosophic or scientific. Is this clear to you, gentlemen?

00:53:36.840 --> 00:53:39.740
It's very simple, this particular

00:53:39.740 --> 00:53:41.020
laws.

00:53:42.320 --> 00:53:43.140
Now comes the Torah

00:53:43.140 --> 00:53:44.960
and it wants to tell you

00:53:44.960 --> 00:53:48.300
that we don't believe this.

00:53:49.200 --> 00:53:50.340
Basically we believe

00:53:50.340 --> 00:53:51.940
that everything,

00:53:52.460 --> 00:53:53.540
not only the substance

00:53:53.540 --> 00:53:56.000
was created by God, but even

00:53:56.000 --> 00:53:58.300
the laws that govern the substance

00:53:58.300 --> 00:54:00.440
are the creation of God.

00:54:00.800 --> 00:54:01.940
God freely

00:54:01.940 --> 00:54:04.160
designed, created,

00:54:04.580 --> 00:54:05.940
implanted, and operated

00:54:05.940 --> 00:54:06.800
this

00:54:06.800 --> 00:54:09.040
this law.

00:54:09.500 --> 00:54:10.700
And if we believe this,

00:54:11.100 --> 00:54:12.740
that everything is the creation of God,

00:54:12.820 --> 00:54:14.260
including the laws of the universe,

00:54:14.780 --> 00:54:16.540
then the whole Torah is very simple in our words.

00:54:16.860 --> 00:54:18.720
God, the whole idea of miracles is simple.

00:54:19.080 --> 00:54:20.900
The whole idea that God chose one nation

00:54:20.900 --> 00:54:22.020
over another is simple.

00:54:22.420 --> 00:54:24.720
The whole idea that there is such a thing as a mitzvot is very simple.

00:54:29.200 --> 00:54:30.540
It pays to study Torah.

00:54:31.140 --> 00:54:32.520
And the proof for it is

00:54:32.520 --> 00:54:34.620
that Sam Leone won the elections.

00:54:36.800 --> 00:54:46.040
I was asked to give you a very short resume of what we studied last week.

00:54:46.040 --> 00:54:51.680
And I think that it's worthwhile to go over it very, very briefly, the main idea, because it's important.

00:54:52.100 --> 00:54:53.800
I think it's the most important idea of the Torah.

00:54:53.980 --> 00:54:56.780
In fact, the book, the Perashat Planeshit, is devoted to this idea.

00:54:57.340 --> 00:54:59.400
What is the basic idea that the Torah wants to teach us?

00:54:59.560 --> 00:55:00.180
It's very simple.

00:55:00.960 --> 00:55:02.300
See, we have misthought.

00:55:02.360 --> 00:55:03.100
We have many commandments.

00:55:03.620 --> 00:55:05.260
Some commandments we don't understand.

00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:10.060
we say, why, who is God to tell us this?

00:55:10.200 --> 00:55:11.900
Even if God tells us, who is God to tell me this?

00:55:12.420 --> 00:55:13.420
I don't want to do it.

00:55:13.900 --> 00:55:15.060
I don't understand this.

00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:16.420
Why me as a Jew?

00:55:16.500 --> 00:55:17.380
Why not the other God?

00:55:18.180 --> 00:55:19.180
And the question that we have,

00:55:19.220 --> 00:55:19.880
all the questions are,

00:55:20.340 --> 00:55:22.180
why would the Jewish people have to do this?

00:55:22.300 --> 00:55:23.160
What's the, you know,

00:55:23.480 --> 00:55:26.000
why we should, after, say, 3,000, 2,000 years,

00:55:26.060 --> 00:55:26.920
do whatever we have to do?

00:55:26.940 --> 00:55:27.200
Why?

00:55:27.680 --> 00:55:29.840
Very difficult question to answer, you know?

00:55:30.340 --> 00:55:33.780
And so these questions are relevant.

00:55:33.780 --> 00:55:34.580
Now that there are,

00:55:35.040 --> 00:55:36.380
it has a very simple thesis.

00:55:36.380 --> 00:55:41.380
This is the problem. You see, the world...

00:55:52.380 --> 00:55:59.380
The world in its entirety, in every part of it, is the creation of God.

00:55:59.380 --> 00:56:01.380
What do we mean by this?

00:56:01.380 --> 00:56:03.380
The coin...

00:56:14.380 --> 00:56:24.380
I want to give you again, in a nutshell, the minikah vasem, so to speak, of the Torah.

00:56:24.380 --> 00:56:30.380
And so if you accept this and you understand it, you'll be able to understand the rest of the Torah.

00:56:30.380 --> 00:56:32.000
of the Torah. And this is,

00:56:32.120 --> 00:56:34.220
subject of this is the Ferasat Beneshit.

00:56:34.580 --> 00:56:35.720
And I tell you what is the main

00:56:35.720 --> 00:56:38.260
basic thought of Judaism.

00:56:39.500 --> 00:56:40.380
First of all, let's

00:56:40.380 --> 00:56:41.480
see a little bit about the Kohen.

00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:43.940
The Kohen, they believe, philosophers

00:56:43.940 --> 00:56:46.240
and scientists, they believe that

00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:47.680
there is a universe. It's true.

00:56:48.680 --> 00:56:49.700
But this universe

00:56:49.700 --> 00:56:52.320
is controlled by certain laws

00:56:52.320 --> 00:56:54.620
of physics. There's the laws of gravity,

00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:55.900
there's the laws of the

00:56:55.900 --> 00:56:57.500
expansion of gases,

00:56:58.240 --> 00:57:00.160
there's the psychological laws that govern

00:57:00.160 --> 00:57:01.880
the human mind, the laws of biology.

00:57:02.620 --> 00:57:04.400
And these laws are

00:57:04.400 --> 00:57:06.460
uncreated.

00:57:07.880 --> 00:57:08.300
They are

00:57:08.300 --> 00:57:10.160
mechanic. Nobody

00:57:10.160 --> 00:57:12.620
could change. And therefore,

00:57:12.780 --> 00:57:13.740
even God himself

00:57:13.740 --> 00:57:15.840
cannot change the laws of gravity.

00:57:16.200 --> 00:57:18.520
God himself cannot change the laws of heredity.

00:57:19.220 --> 00:57:20.100
The laws of

00:57:20.100 --> 00:57:21.780
chemistry.

00:57:22.360 --> 00:57:24.100
It cannot be changed. This is the way the thing is.

00:57:25.020 --> 00:57:25.960
And therefore, they say,

00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:28.160
the universe is certain billions of years

00:57:28.160 --> 00:57:31.500
because according to this law, this is what it takes the universe to be created.

00:57:32.380 --> 00:57:33.080
It is very simple.

00:57:33.380 --> 00:57:37.380
You take a piece of tree, and how long will it take this tree to become a diamond?

00:57:38.100 --> 00:57:39.160
Several billion years.

00:57:39.700 --> 00:57:43.180
So therefore, you have a diamond, there is a proof that this is several billion years.

00:57:43.300 --> 00:57:44.080
And this is a simple example.

00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:46.300
So what does it mean, this?

00:57:46.400 --> 00:57:48.980
It means more that there is such a thing as a universe.

00:57:49.380 --> 00:57:51.840
It means that there is a kind of determinism.

00:57:52.620 --> 00:57:54.880
And we must be what we are.

00:57:55.360 --> 00:57:57.400
And we don't have a freedom of choice.

00:57:57.400 --> 00:58:02.260
And, for instance, this idea of, say, of physics, this scientific idea,

00:58:02.420 --> 00:58:04.400
it's been said to say in our country, to the social realm.

00:58:05.080 --> 00:58:10.520
For instance, they say, well, this young man or this young girl is a delinquent.

00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:11.920
Well, it's not their fault.

00:58:12.000 --> 00:58:13.400
It's the condition of the social environment.

00:58:13.580 --> 00:58:14.260
It's this and this one.

00:58:14.400 --> 00:58:17.760
So try to say why he had to act in this way, you know?

00:58:17.920 --> 00:58:20.720
And actually, he's the victim of a situation.

00:58:21.140 --> 00:58:22.460
I don't know whether I'm clear or not.

00:58:22.540 --> 00:58:24.460
You know, in other words, there is a certain thing as laws,

00:58:24.900 --> 00:58:26.860
and we are the subject of these laws.

00:58:27.400 --> 00:58:30.780
And our freedom is very, very limited.

00:58:31.280 --> 00:58:35.800
If you are in Islam, then you must come out like everybody else.

00:58:35.880 --> 00:58:36.800
There's no such a thing, you know.

00:58:37.020 --> 00:58:41.980
So that's the way, the philosophy of the boy who goes.

00:58:42.420 --> 00:58:45.100
We, as Jews, we reject this.

00:58:45.940 --> 00:58:51.860
We believe that not only the substance, matter as such, is the creation of God.

00:58:51.860 --> 00:58:56.260
Not only that God made from zero something with three dimensions called matter,

00:58:56.260 --> 00:59:02.000
but also all the laws, even the most basic laws of the universe, were created by God.

00:59:02.320 --> 00:59:04.360
What does it mean that they were created by God?

00:59:04.820 --> 00:59:08.620
It means that God, as a free author, made these laws.

00:59:09.120 --> 00:59:11.400
He could change them whenever he wishes.

00:59:12.120 --> 00:59:16.700
For us, the miracle, the nest, is the proof.

00:59:17.780 --> 00:59:24.140
It's evidence to the fact that God, author of the laws of nature, could change them whenever he wishes.

00:59:24.820 --> 00:59:26.960
He is the absolute master of the universe.

00:59:27.460 --> 00:59:32.640
There is nothing that in any way restricts, controls, or limits his absolute power.

00:59:34.480 --> 00:59:40.900
Notice, God is not the pilot driving a jet, as the Lord would say.

00:59:42.360 --> 00:59:45.600
Which, a pilot driving a jet, of course, can use the jet as a submarine.

00:59:45.880 --> 00:59:51.520
In a way, the pilot who's driving this jet is limited by the jet.

00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:58.140
And the God conceives God as, say, a big pilot, a big scientist controlling, you know, the universe.

00:59:58.240 --> 01:00:01.900
But the universe is what it is, and God cannot do with the universe more than what the universe is.

01:00:02.040 --> 01:00:04.180
He is in a way limited by the universe.

01:00:04.300 --> 01:00:05.580
This is the way the God conceives it.

01:00:06.140 --> 01:00:06.780
We say no.

01:00:07.560 --> 01:00:10.900
God is in no way controlled by the universe.

01:00:11.780 --> 01:00:13.380
And therefore we begin with the first thing,

01:00:13.480 --> 01:00:15.480
Vereshit v'al Elohim et ha-shamayim v'ha'aret.

01:00:16.020 --> 01:00:17.280
So the shamayim v'ha'aret.

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:22.720
And we don't mean the material heaven and the material earth,

01:00:23.040 --> 01:00:30.540
but we mean rather the laws, even the laws, the basic laws governing this universe are the creation of God.

01:00:30.660 --> 01:00:31.720
An example of it.

01:00:32.640 --> 01:00:33.360
There was Hosea.

01:00:33.600 --> 01:00:34.340
There was darkness.

01:00:34.500 --> 01:00:35.160
Absolute darkness.

01:00:36.280 --> 01:00:38.680
And then God creates light.

01:00:39.920 --> 01:00:43.040
So, if you have light, today you say,

01:00:43.040 --> 01:00:48.080
If you have light, naturally, of course, there is no darkness.

01:00:48.720 --> 01:00:50.400
There cannot be light and darkness together.

01:00:50.520 --> 01:00:51.240
That's obvious.

01:00:52.300 --> 01:00:54.160
But come to the line, it tells you something very, very deep.

01:00:54.380 --> 01:00:54.400
It says,

01:00:54.640 --> 01:01:01.160
This, that there is light and darkness cannot be together.

01:01:01.780 --> 01:01:03.180
This is also a creation of God.

01:01:04.320 --> 01:01:07.020
If God would have wanted there to be dark and light together,

01:01:07.320 --> 01:01:08.100
how? We don't know.

01:01:08.180 --> 01:01:10.280
Our mind today does not operate according to those laws.

01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:10.860
You see?

01:01:10.860 --> 01:01:12.700
But even by Abdel Elohim,

01:01:12.820 --> 01:01:14.900
even the very

01:01:14.900 --> 01:01:16.260
contradiction

01:01:16.260 --> 01:01:17.160
between

01:01:17.160 --> 01:01:21.060
light and darkness,

01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:22.360
this contradiction,

01:01:22.920 --> 01:01:24.660
it is not an accident,

01:01:24.800 --> 01:01:26.500
it is not nature or necessary so.

01:01:26.820 --> 01:01:28.520
It is also the creation of God.

01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:32.880
So, without creation

01:01:32.880 --> 01:01:35.060
of God, everything

01:01:35.060 --> 01:01:35.720
would have been

01:01:35.720 --> 01:01:39.020
God created the world.

01:01:39.020 --> 01:01:50.360
In its first state, without laws of nature, the whole universe was in a complete chaos.

01:01:50.740 --> 01:01:53.980
Because there was no laws of nature to govern this universe.

01:01:54.760 --> 01:01:57.680
And the laws of nature came as a step further.

01:02:00.020 --> 01:02:00.960
It's very important.

01:02:01.360 --> 01:02:05.940
Now, if we accept the thesis of the Torah, then the whole Judaism is very clear.

01:02:05.940 --> 01:02:09.300
Even if I cannot understand why I have to put the feeling

01:02:09.300 --> 01:02:11.320
But if I recognize

01:02:11.320 --> 01:02:13.140
That I think as an author of the universe

01:02:13.140 --> 01:02:15.400
Who is absolute master of everything

01:02:15.400 --> 01:02:16.440
And is telling me put the feeling

01:02:16.440 --> 01:02:17.780
I have to accept it

01:02:17.780 --> 01:02:19.500
I happen to be his subject

01:02:19.500 --> 01:02:23.280
I cannot say well you know God I don't need you

01:02:23.280 --> 01:02:24.980
Because there is laws of the universe

01:02:24.980 --> 01:02:25.800
That you cannot change

01:02:25.800 --> 01:02:27.760
And whether you want it or not you are stuck with me

01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:29.740
We cannot say this according to Judaism

01:02:29.740 --> 01:02:32.440
Simply we are

01:02:32.440 --> 01:02:35.120
If we recognize that he is the absolute master

01:02:35.120 --> 01:02:37.880
then we have to give absolute obedience.

01:02:38.800 --> 01:02:39.640
Now, some people say,

01:02:39.680 --> 01:02:40.880
I don't want to accept this. Fine!

01:02:41.160 --> 01:02:42.520
But this is the thesis of Judaism.

01:02:42.920 --> 01:02:44.860
The thesis of Judaism is a very simple thesis.

01:02:45.920 --> 01:02:47.040
Is it clear to you, gentlemen?

01:02:47.440 --> 01:02:49.920
Now, let me tell you something.

01:02:50.020 --> 01:02:51.060
I have to give you a step further

01:02:51.060 --> 01:02:52.020
before we go into the interpretation

01:02:52.020 --> 01:02:54.840
because it's important for a clean understanding of, you know,

01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:56.900
I know that everybody agrees with me,

01:02:56.900 --> 01:02:58.240
including myself, but so what?

01:03:01.420 --> 01:03:02.400
Let me tell you something.

01:03:03.060 --> 01:03:04.500
See, in a way, you must understand

01:03:04.500 --> 01:03:05.980
What the Torah is telling you in this parashit,

01:03:06.020 --> 01:03:09.440
it's very important that you see.

01:03:09.740 --> 01:03:10.580
What do you see from this?

01:03:11.300 --> 01:03:12.980
The first stage,

01:03:14.480 --> 01:03:17.600
universe in its first status was tov v'voh, chaos.

01:03:18.540 --> 01:03:19.640
After this, there's laws.

01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:21.680
And laws establish order in the chaos.

